From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: offload authorized wireless bridge flows

Mark NFPROTO_BRIDGE flow rules explicitly and preserve their Ethernet
addresses and IPv4 TTL / IPv6 hop limit. Keep route admission separate.
Require both authorized wireless forward paths, full source/destination
MAC matches and station epochs before learning an IPv4 or IPv6 row.

Withdraw pending and bound entries for either peer on revocation.
Synchronize bridge port, VLAN, FDB, STP and isolation policy changes
with software flow generations and hardware invalidation. Stop both PPE
engines on an invalidation failure before releasing affected cookies.

Allow same-port paths only with hairpin enabled, support RCU callers of
the bridge state accessor, and reject stale rules without reporting
hardware success. Serialize statistics with atomic invalidation.
Index each bridge cookie before exposing its RX candidate, and remove
the index if publication fails, so allocation failure cannot leave an
unowned hardware binding.

Always detach an unregistering bridge port even when hardware quiescence
fails: NETDEV_UNREGISTER cannot be rejected. Keep the generation blocked
through nested detach changes, retain uncertain PPE owners, and preserve
normal user-initiated delif error handling.

The CT route-format FOE entries used for bridging rewrite the complete
IPv4 DS field or IPv6 traffic class from their output field. Keep that
field zero and require the companion NPU receive guard before accepting
or learning a wireless bridge flow. The guard checks every packet before
TDMA, including packets belonging to an already bound flow: Ethernet
frames shorter than 72 bytes and packets with any nonzero DSCP or ECN
bits take the existing host path. Eligible packets with a zero DS field
can still use hardware, even when the same five-tuple also carries marked
packets. Software bridge flow forwarding preserves the original DS field,
TTL / hop limit, addresses and checksums. Wired bridge ingress remains
unsupported by this hardware path.

Publish BR_FLOW_OFFLOAD_API for guarded mac80211 integration, plus the
NPU receive-guard readiness contract implemented by the next patch.

